wayland: present through wl_shm when the host has no zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1

Applies to aquamarine v0.15.1 (f31c47a1b9d300847d8fc3108ad959448103dfc1) with
`git apply` at the repo root.

Without zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 the Wayland backend used to refuse to start
("Missing protocols"), leaving no DRM fd and no allocator. With this patch it
falls back to wl_shm presentation ("wl_shm mode"):

- start(): the dmabuf requirement is dropped. Without a usable
  zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 (or with AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_PRESENT=1) the backend opens the
  render node AQ_WAYLAND_RENDER_NODE (default /dev/dri/renderD128; render
  nodes only). That fd feeds the GBM allocator and the consumer's renderer as
  before.
- Render formats become XRGB8888 and ARGB8888 with DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR only,
  so the CPU can read the buffers. GBM allocates them with RENDERING only
  (no SCANOUT) in this mode.
- commit() never blocks on the GPU. The frame becomes pending and stays in
  flight (no frame event, no rendering into the swapchain) until it reaches
  the host. Its explicit in-fence is dup'ed into an epoll set whose fd is one
  of pollFDs(); when it signals, only the damaged rectangles are copied
  (gbm_bo_map by default, or a dmabuf mmap bracketed by DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC
  with AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_MMAP=1) into one of at most 3 memfd wl_shm buffers,
  which is attached with wl_surface.damage for exactly what changed. Buffers
  the host still holds are never written; a frame waits for a
  wl_buffer.release instead. No fence or syncobj is ever created or exported.
- A commit without changes re-attaches an up-to-date buffer with one pixel of
  damage, so the host always gets a normal buffer commit and answers its
  frame callback. No commit is sent without an attach.
- Frames without a fence are copied after DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC(START|READ) and
  the copied pixels are read again 25 ms later (a timerfd in the same epoll
  set), or with the next frame if it comes first.
- test() rejects buffers that are not this backend's LINEAR swapchain buffers,
  so a consumer's direct scanout of client buffers never engages.
- No hardware cursor in wl_shm mode (capabilities() = 0). The consumer draws
  the cursor and the host's pointer image is hidden on enter.
- In wl_shm mode, xdg_toplevel.configure is applied after its
  xdg_surface.configure is acked, so no buffer reaches an unconfigured surface.
- No dmabuf proxy is dereferenced when the host lacks the global (setCursor,
  CWaylandBuffer).
- GBM: drmGetDeviceNameFromFd2() may return NULL (no uevent in sysfs). It was
  assigned to a std::string unchecked.

With a working zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 and AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_PRESENT unset,
behaviour is unchanged. The only exception is the NULL check above.

New environment variables are documented in docs/env.md.

