index b496edb..50a1108 100644
--- a/docs/env.md
+++ b/docs/env.md
@@ -16,3 +16,11 @@ Unless specified otherwise, a variable is enabled if and only if it's set to `1`
 ### Debugging
 
 `AQ_TRACE` -> Enables trace (very verbose) logging
+
+### Wayland
+
+`AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_PRESENT` -> Present output frames to the host compositor as wl_shm copies. Used automatically when the host has no (working) `zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1`; `1` forces it, `0` disables it.
+`AQ_WAYLAND_RENDER_NODE` -> In wl_shm mode, the DRM render node to allocate and render on. Default `/dev/dri/renderD128`. Only render nodes are accepted.
+`AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_MMAP` -> In wl_shm mode, `1` reads rendered buffers through a direct mmap of the dmabuf instead of `gbm_bo_map` (the default).
+`AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_DMABUF_SYNC` -> In wl_shm mode, bracket reads with `DMA_BUF_IOCTL_SYNC`: unset for frames without a fence, re-copies and direct mmap reads; `1` always; `0` never.
+`AQ_WAYLAND_SHM_RECOPY` -> In wl_shm mode, read pixels again one host frame later: unset only for frames without a fence; `1` every frame; `0` never.
